# ── Chapter 10 fidelity pins: "Contribution" ─────────────────────────────────
#
# KIND: CONTENT pin. Run:
#   nibli-pin --kb new-book-plans/constitution.nibli book-1/10-contribution.pins.nibli
#
# The chapter's central claim — that recognition has no quantity, and is never
# ranked — is a claim about an ABSENCE and so cannot be pinned by a query. It is
# checked structurally instead, by the guards in verify.sh section 4 — listed here
# without a count, because this list has already grown once since it was written:
#   - no digit in an enacted line          (a quantity cannot be written)
#   - nothing reads `reward`               (recognition feeds nothing downstream)
#   - no rule joins `teaches` or `work` with itself
#                                          (a quantity cannot be counted either)
# The last two are the "What is lost" section: degree is available here and is
# refused, not merely unbuilt. Do not weaken them without rewriting :112-138.
#
# A FOURTH GUARD, verify.sh section 4a: `reward` is arity 1 by decision. Giving it
# a second place to record what the recognition was minted FOR — provenance — is
# refused (2026-08-01, reasoning in CLAUDE.md). It defends :19-21 and :105
# directly: arity 2 makes recognition a fact about a person AND a source, which is
# no longer "the same single fact".
#
# WHY IT IS IN verify.sh AND NOT LEFT TO THESE PINS. The three TRUE pins below do
# catch a rewrite of the heads — measured, `reward(Esa/Quin/Gia)` flip FALSE. But
# the three FALSE pins cannot catch anything: under arity 2 `reward/1` stops
# existing, so they keep answering FALSE and keep passing, against a relation that
# is no longer there. Two more pins elsewhere go vacuous the same way,
# `reward(Cira)` in 06-clawback and `reward(Dev)` in rights-floor. And the ADDITIVE
# shape is invisible to every pin in the suite: a fourth head at arity 2 beside the
# three leaves `reward/1` deriving and everything green. Never let this file drift
# to FALSE-only pins on `reward`.

:expect-pins 12

# "Esa taught Fin, and is recognised."
? teaches(Esa, Fin).
# => TRUE

? reward(Esa).
# => TRUE

# "Quin did the census, and is recognised."
? work(Quin, Census).
# => TRUE

? reward(Quin).
# => TRUE

# "Gia examined Bela's conduct without deceit, and is recognised."
? judge(Gia, Bela).
# => TRUE

? capture(Gia, Bela).
# => TRUE

? reward(Gia).
# => TRUE

# "Bela taught Cira — a real act ... Bela is not recognised, because Bela was
#  voided. The teaching happened and produces nothing."
? teaches(Bela, Cira).
# => TRUE

? false(Bela).
# => TRUE

? reward(Bela).
# => FALSE

# "Lupo examined Mira and lied about it, and earns nothing"
? reward(Lupo).
# => FALSE

# "Dev judged his own child ... earns nothing either"
? reward(Dev).
# => FALSE
